  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Portfolio Project**\n\nI\'m starting a new personal portfolio project using React/TypeScript. The goal is to highlight my experience as a Solution Architect with over 11 years in Telecom, focusing on OSS/BSS. I\'m excited to showcase my skills effectively.\n\n\n**Refining Requirements Gathering**\n\nI\'m now revisiting the user\'s detailed request. My focus shifts to understanding the specific demands, particularly regarding design elements, content management, and security. I\'m taking notes on each requirement, making sure I don\'t overlook a critical piece of the project.\n\n\n**Evaluating Project\'s Technical Scope**\n\nI\'m evaluating the scope, now, including Firebase integration for the database and authentication, along with the Gemini API for AI features. It looks like it\'ll be a good way to showcase some skills. I want to build a secure backend to securely manage the dynamic content, and implement Firebase Firestore and Auth for persistent storage and an admin dashboard.\n\n\n**Adding AI Chat Feature**\n\nI\'m now thinking about integrating a slick AI chat feature using the Gemini API, server-side. It would be an assistant visitors can converse with about my expertise! I\'m nixing OAuth, workspace integrations, real-time capabilities and image generation. Considering custom Tailwind UI is a good alternative.\n\nI\'m going to do a skill check next, listing my skills from the SKILL.md and marking the relevant ones. I\'ll take a look at the project\'s files before making changes. After that I have to check the `.env.example` file and the `package.json` file. Looks like I have the packages I need.\n\n\n"
