  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Persistence & Blueprint**\n\nI\'m now weighing the user\'s need for database persistence, which will heavily impact the architectural design. Before moving forward with Firebase Blueprint setup or server configuration, I need to know if we need it. This factor dictates the complexity of the admin dashboard and how content is managed long term.\n\n\n**Analyzing Security Setup**\n\nI\'m now focusing on secure backend setup, specifically around Firebase. I\'m considering using `set_up_firebase` and analyzing the `userConfirmedTermsAcceptedInUI` parameter. My initial idea was to prevent a UI prompt, but now I\'m thinking of alternative setups: integrating Firebase as a layer, or a fully functional local client-side storage + server-side storage system that can integrate Firebase as a layer.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Firestore & Blueprint**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing Firestore and the `firebase-blueprint.json` file. It\'s clear that cloud persistence via Firestore is essential for Vetrivel\'s portfolio and the Admin Dashboard. I need to make sure their projects and blog posts don\'t disappear on rebuilds. Now, I will design the `firebase-blueprint.json` file.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the `firebase-blueprint.json` file to plan our Firestore data model under the `firebase-integration` skill. This file specifies our entities (projects, blogs, and messages) and maps them to Firestore collections."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 937197792
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
