    thinking: "**Awaiting Firebase Setup**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag. The tool is requesting Firebase configuration and showing its UI. The instructions now direct me to pause processing until the user interacts with the Firebase setup. I am currently holding on this point.\n\n\n**Considering User Response**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user interaction after the \"continue\" prompt. My understanding is that \"continue\" suggests either an acceptance of terms (likely happening behind the scenes in the Firebase UI) or a desire to move forward with the build. A critical question is whether `firebase-applet-config.json` is present. If not, I am exploring a dual-mode database service. This architecture would gracefully shift between local, mock-free state (localStorage or a node-based JSON database) and Firebase based on the config file\'s existence.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Feature Development**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s feature requests, aiming for rapid implementation. The immediate goal is a secure, Express API with local persistence for project and blog management and contacts. This local data storage uses files like `/data/projects.json`. I\'m also planning to check for the `firebase-applet-config.json` to enable cloud support as a later upgrade. The design focus is on a clean, responsive, mobile-first design with a dark mode toggle. I\'ll be prioritizing: a project gallery, a blog, a contact form, and a custom Gemini assistant.\n\n\n**Defining Core Architecture**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the technical implementation. I\'m focusing on key features: a gorgeous, beautifully styled chatbot, sleek page transitions, integrated social links, and a functional search bar for navigating the site\'s content. I\'m thinking about structuring the project files. I\'ll need a `/src/types.ts` for data definitions, and a `/server.ts` for a secure backend. The backend will support Vite middleware and secure REST API endpoints for project management, blog posts, and contact submissions. I am starting by considering the project and blog post endpoints.\n\n\n**Outlining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now outlining API endpoints in detail. The plan includes secure `/api/projects`, `/api/blogs`, and `/api/messages` routes. These endpoints will feature admin auth for POST, PUT, and DELETE operations. There is also an `/api/admin/login` and an `/api/chat` route using the `@google/genai` Gemini SDK for an AI assistant. I\'ve designed the `/api/chat` endpoint to utilize `gemini-3.5-flash` for a fast Q&A experience.\n\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the `/src/types.ts` file to model the data entities of Vetrivel\'s portfolio: Projects, Blog posts, Messages, Admin authentication state, and chat interactions. This establishes strong typing across the client and server."
    thinking_duration {
