  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Firestore Limits**\n\nOkay, I\'m now digging into the specifics of Firestore quotas within the AI Studio environment. It seems that when a user bumps up against a limit, there\'s a pretty clear \"Quota exceeded\" error, and it specifies that the quota resets daily. I think providing the user with explicit instructions on how to locate detailed quota information within the Spark plan could be very useful for these edge cases.\n\n\n**Clarifying Quota Reset Times**\n\nI\'m focusing now on how to best explain the Firebase/Firestore quota reset process to the user, particularly after a \"Quota exceeded\" error. The user is asking \"when will it reset?\" so I want to ensure they receive a helpful answer, even if they had a previous error, I want to clarify how to find their database. I\'m also examining the `/` directory to see if there are other relevant files.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Config File Absence**\n\nI\'ve determined `firebase-applet-config.json` isn\'t in `/`, which suggests the Firebase setup might be incomplete or cancelled, or the user is likely asking about daily quota resets. I\'m now clear on that. It\'s midnight Pacific Time (PST/PDT), or 24 hours. The user can find quota details under the Spark plan of the Enterprise section of the Firebase Pricing page.\n\n\n**Addressing User Portfolio Needs**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s explicit request for a personal portfolio website, alongside the earlier error message and the ongoing quota questions. It seems there\'s a disconnect. I must now consider the user\'s initial error, quota details and also the personal portfolio project requirements, while adhering to the instructions to finish the scope, and that the user wants me to build their portfolio! I\'ll outline the required subtasks, in sequence, to ensure that the user\'s project is completed.\n\n\n**Designing Portfolio Framework**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on building a responsive, minimalist portfolio for Vetrivel Muthusamy, a Solution Architect. The `/src` directory is empty, so I need to implement a full application from scratch. This includes a secure backend, admin dashboard with dark mode support, and comprehensive documentation to ensure it scales. I must ensure the portfolio perfectly matches the specified requirements!\n\n\n**Expanding Portfolio Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial features into the portfolio design. I\'m excited about including a gallery, contact form, and blog. I\'m also planning for a dark mode toggle with full accessibility and prioritizing fast loading speeds and SEO optimization. Smooth transitions are essential, alongside social media links and a search bar for easy navigation. A secure admin dashboard is the goal, capable of managing content using local storage. Crucially, I\'m designing a dual-mode state manager for seamless operation with or without Firebase. I\'m also planning a detailed developer documentation section in the admin dashboard.\n\n\n**Examining Source Directory**\n\nI\'m now examining the `/src` directory\'s contents, particularly `package.json`, to determine the existing tools. I can see the app uses React, TailwindCSS, and several UI libraries. I\'ve noted the lack of a markdown parser but I\'m prepared to create a lightweight custom renderer, or install a third-party module if preferred. I am planning on using React types!\n\n\n**Developing Core Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the essential building blocks of the portfolio. I am designing several key components. I\'m building `Navbar`, `Hero`, `ProjectGallery`, `BlogSection`, and `ContactForm`. I am also planning on incorporating an AI twin feature with a search bar and a robust backend to address security vulnerabilities. I\'m keen on including input sanitization, secure HTML rendering, and proper password hashing. I\'ll include secure session tokens, preventing unsafe eval, and ensure safe localStorage parsing.\n\n\n**Inspecting Admin Components**\n\nI\'m now examining the `AdminDashboard` and `DevDocs` components, noting their roles in managing content and providing developer guidance. I\'m building a robust `storage.ts` module, which will leverage local storage with pre-populated data to give Vetrivel\'s portfolio a rich initial experience. I\'ve confirmed `motion` is pre-installed.\n\n\n**Implementing Animation and Imports**\n\nI\'m now implementing `motion/react` for animations as instructed, using `import { motion, AnimatePresence } from \"motion/react\";`. I\'m also ensuring proper Lucide icon imports. Next, I am creating `/src/db/storage.ts` to hold database types and pre-seeded data for the portfolio. I am preparing the data for the projects, blog posts, contact messages, and admin credentials, using secure client-side state management. I will ensure that Vetrivel Muthusamy\'s portfolio shines right away!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 28
      nanos: 390989683
    }
