  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering PDF Integration**\n\nI\'m currently focused on seamlessly integrating a high-fidelity PDF export feature for the portfolio/resume. Initial considerations revolve around incorporating a prominent \"EXPORT PDF\" button, perhaps within the `Navbar.tsx` component, to ensure easy access for visitors seeking a professional PDF version.\n\n\n**Designing Resume Modal**\n\nI\'m now designing the `/src/components/ResumeModal.tsx`. It will house an interactive resume customizer and exporter, styled to resemble a crisp, professional, clean layout\342\200\224an \"Architect style\" with a grid. This is meant to be a great Architect\'s Resume Generator, and will be triggered by an export button. I\'m focusing on the UX within the modal itself. I\'m also planning to add this as a secondary action in the `Hero.tsx` component as well.\n\n\n**Refining PDF Customization**\n\nI\'m presently refining the PDF customization features. The focus is now on incorporating theme choices within the modal, specifically \"Contemporary Blue Blueprint\" and \"Classic Corporate Schwarz\". I\'m implementing feature flags for profile cover, sub-narratives, project breakdown, and contact details. A progress bar simulating PDF generation will precede a print-optimized output, ensuring a clean A4 format PDF using browser print functionality.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Print-Friendly Design**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing a clean `@media print` layout within `ResumeModal.tsx`. It\'s going to generate a reliable, high-quality, and fast print view, which circumvents potential issues with external PDF libraries in sandboxed environments. The layout will clearly showcase the user\'s experience and qualifications, and offer user-selectable content checkboxes to tailor the output.\n\n\n**Exploring PDF Delivery Options**\n\nI\'m now exploring multiple PDF delivery methods. I\'m thinking we can offer both a static, downloadable PDF and a dynamic, customizable PDF generator! The former ensures a clean, pre-compiled resume download, while the latter allows for personalized print-friendly output client-side, opening a new window or utilizing print styles for clean rendering. This will all be in the new `ResumeModal.tsx` file. Now, I\'m focusing on crafting the initial resume content within `ResumeModal.tsx`, using Vetrivel\'s provided details as a starting point.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create a highly advanced, fully interactive, and visually stunning `ResumeModal.tsx` component. It includes a custom resume designer/customizer for recruiters (letting them toggle specific modules like \"Tech Stack Grid\", \"Key Outage Cases\", \"Timeline\", etc.), a direct printable engine that strips out all website components to generate a pristine, print-perfect standard PDF, and styling options matching the \"Architect\" design aesthetic."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 739678748
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
