  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Theme Toggle**\n\nOkay, I\'m thinking about a professional light/dark/system toggle within `Navbar.tsx`. Instead of a simple boolean for dark mode, I\'ve moved to a `ThemeMode` type with \"light\", \"dark\", and \"system\" options. Initializing the state with a function that determines the default theme is next.\n\n\n**Implementing System Preferences**\n\nI\'ve realized I need to account for system preferences when the theme mode is set to \"system\". I\'m now crafting a `useEffect` hook to dynamically apply the theme based on the user\'s system settings. Inside the effect, I will check the `themeMode` to determine if system preferences are needed, then apply the correct `dark` class to the root element. I will also persist the theme mode to local storage, and add a media query listener for system changes when applicable.\n\n\n**Selecting Theme Icons**\n\nI\'m now focused on the visual design, specifically the theme switcher\'s UI. I\'m exploring icon options for a light/dark/system toggle. I\'m currently leaning towards an elegant dropdown with a clear, concise micro-segmented control that feels \"premium.\" I\'m evaluating the aesthetic of a neat inline list versus a small dropdown menu for the theme modes. I think an icon that rolls down would be very intuitive.\n\n\n"
