  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Key Technologies**\n\nOkay, I\'ve confirmed the initial assessment is positive. Now, I\'m diving deeper, and identifying the key technologies needed for the Portfolio redesign. Specifically, the latest technologies: Java 17/21, Spring Boot 3.x, and REST API & Microservices with Spring Web Flux. These will be the foundation.\n\n\n**Expanding Technical Scope**\n\nI\'m now expanding the technology considerations. I\'m focusing on Spring Cloud, React 18+ with Vite, TypeScript and Tailwind. I\'m also ensuring alignment with TM Forum Open APIs and Agile methodologies (CSPO). Cloud platforms (AWS, Docker, Kubernetes) and comprehensive testing architectures (Selenium Grid, Cucumber, Postman, JUnit, Mockito) are critical. Furthermore, I\'m defining visual improvements: `InteractiveBlueprint.tsx` will highlight physical parameters, `Hero.tsx` will explicitly list the mentioned platforms, and `ResumeModal.tsx` will showcase the modern tech stacks. A redesign with premium aesthetics is also needed.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Control**\n\nI\'m now focused on implementing theme control. My plan is to add a dropdown to the Navbar, allowing users to select \"Light Mode,\" \"Dark Mode,\" or \"System Preference.\" This will be in `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`. The dropdown will be visually appealing with active mode indicators. I\'ll dynamically update the `html` classes using custom listeners to achieve dynamic theme changes. It must look like a \"Theme Control Protocol\" console dropdown.\n\nI\'m considering a custom notification system for the footer email link in `App.tsx` or a dedicated Footer component, or simple React State inside a brand new custom Footer component! When they click, they will get feedback.\n\n\n**Refining Theme Integration**\n\nI\'m now refining the theme integration within `Navbar.tsx`. Instead of a boolean, I\'m using a `ThemeMode` type with \"light,\" \"dark,\" and \"system\" options. The code is being updated to reflect this change. I\'m also preparing to develop the dropdown\'s custom design. Additionally, I\'m thinking about including a custom, animated toast message that shows up in the bottom right corner when users copy my email address from the footer.\n\n\n**Managing Theme Preferences**\n\nI\'m now focusing on persistence and system preference integration. I\'m using `localStorage` to save the selected theme mode (\"light\", \"dark\", or \"system\") and initializing the theme from saved data. I\'m implementing a `useEffect` hook to apply the theme based on the selected mode and system preferences, ensuring a seamless experience.\n\n\n**Refining Theme Control**\n\nI\'m now refining the theme control, and I\'m tackling the self-closing menu issue for the custom dropdown. I\'m leaning toward a hover-dropdown or small clickable popover, ideally positioned absolutely. The dropdown will toggle `isThemeMenuOpen`, and a backdrop (or mouse-leave event) will close it. Considering a segmented group layout in the navbar to check horizontal space with items!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will edit `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` to implement a highly robust \"Light / Dark / System\" switcher with a dropdown menu selector, active indicator tags, and system color listening logic. Let\'s first edit the imports and the raw state hook of `Navbar.tsx`."
