  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Server Implementation**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation details of `/server.ts` to fully integrate the server with Vite middleware. I\'m focusing on how to configure this within Express, drawing from the Full-Stack Apps guide for guidance on setting up the Vite middleware. The goal is a seamless server-client interaction.\n\n\n**Initializing API Functionality**\n\nI\'ve just integrated the Google GenAI library and set up the initial structure for the `/api/chat` route using Express. I\'m focusing on parsing the incoming request body, specifically the `messages` array, to ensure it meets the expected format. I\'m building out error handling to ensure invalid payloads are gracefully rejected, and the request is rejected with a 400 error. I\'m formulating an approach to properly convert these messages into the format required by the Gemini API.\n\n\n**Highlighting Key Accomplishments**\n\nI\'m synthesizing a summary of Vetrivel\'s impressive background to highlight key accomplishments. I\'m focusing on quantifying the impact of his work at Capgemini, emphasizing the 40% reduction in regression duration achieved through his Selenium Grid design. The goal is to showcase his deep expertise in Java, REST APIs, Docker, and AWS EKS, as well as TM Forum standards and billing assurance, which prevented millions in revenue leakage. I am also highlighting his web frontend skills.\n\n\n**Refining Content Formatting**\n\nI\'m now focusing on formatting content for the **Gemini API**. I\'ve created a clean, legible Markdown format and I\'m ensuring all answers are friendly and direct. I am also highlighting key words in **bold**. My aim is to correctly map the user and model roles to ensure data compatibility. I\'m focusing on the mapping of the \'assistant\' role to \'model\' for Gemini alignment.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 943242126
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
