    modified_response: "I have analyzed and resolved the issue causing the **404 (Not Found)** error on your GitHub Pages deployment.\n\n### \360\237\224\215 Cause of the 404 Error\nGitHub Pages is a static hosting platform. Because your repository contained raw source files, the browser downloaded the unbuilt `index.html` which requested the raw source file `/src/main.tsx`. Browsers cannot run raw TypeScript source code directly. Additionally, the absolute root slash `/` in the script source caused it to look at the absolute root domain (`https://vetrivelm02.github.io/src/main.tsx`) rather than the correct repository subfolder (`https://vetrivelm02.github.io/vetrivel-portfolio/...`).\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\233\240\357\270\217 What I Implemented to Fix This\n\n1. **Relative Base Path Mapping**: Configured the build parameters so all compiled static assets are bundled with relative paths (`./`) instead of absolute paths (`/`). This ensures correct loading from any custom domain subfolder like `/vetrivel-portfolio/` without requiring hardcoded configuration.\n2. **Automated CI/CD Workflow**: Created an elegant **GitHub Actions workflow**. Whenever you push changes to your `main` or `master` branch, GitHub will automatically trigger a clean build process, compile the static files into `dist/`, and deploy the production-ready build to GitHub Pages.\n3. **Optimized Chatbot Fallback**: Refined the AI assistant\'s network fallback behavior. If a visitor opens the chatbot on the static GitHub Pages deployment (where the live backend is resting), the bot will gracefully provide your direct, clickable email, phone, and professional LinkedIn/GitHub contacts.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\232\200 How to Enable the Automated Deployment on GitHub\n\nTo activate the automatic builder on your GitHub repository:\n1. Push these updated files to your GitHub repository.\n2. Go to your repository on GitHub.\n3. Click on the **Settings** tab.\n4. On the left sidebar, click **Pages** (under the \"Code and automation\" section).\n5. Under **Build and deployment**, change the **Source** dropdown from *Deploy from a branch* to **GitHub Actions**.\n\nOnce selected, GitHub will automatically run the new pipeline and deploy your portfolio seamlessly!"
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 135052482
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
