  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Diagnosing Job Failure**\n\nI\'m currently investigating why a specific GitHub Action job, particularly the static page deploy, isn\'t running. The error message indicates an account lock as the culprit. I\'m focusing on verifying the account\'s status, checking recent activity for any unusual patterns that might trigger a lock, and reviewing the Action\'s configuration for potential permission issues.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The error **\"The job was not started because your account is locked due to a billing issue\"** is a GitHub-specific account restriction. It indicates that GitHub has paused your automated workflows (GitHub Actions) either because:\n1. Your GitHub account has a billing hold (e.g., an outstanding balance or an expired payment method on file).\n2. Your monthly allowance of free GitHub Actions runner minutes (typically 2,000 minutes/month for free accounts) has been completely exhausted.\n\nSince this issue is on GitHub\'s side, here are the steps to resolve it:\n\n### 1. Check and Resolve GitHub Billing (Recommended)\n1. Go to your [GitHub Billing Settings](https://github.com/settings/billing).\n2. Check for any alerts regarding:\n   - **Payment Information**: Ensure your card on file is up-to-date.\n   - **Actions Minutes**: Check if you have exceeded your free tier limit. If so, you can add a small spending limit (e.g., $1) to resume workflows immediately.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Alternative: Manual Deploy to GitHub Pages (Without GitHub Actions)\nIf you don\'t want to deal with GitHub Actions billing right now, you can build and publish the app directly from your terminal or upload the static files manually.\n\n#### Option A: Deploy using the `gh-pages` npm package\n1. Download or clone your repository to your local machine.\n2. Install the `gh-pages` package:\n   ```bash\n   npm install gh-pages --save-dev\n   ```\n3. Add these scripts to your `package.json`:\n   ```json\n   \"scripts\": {\n     \"predeploy\": \"npm run build\",\n     \"deploy\": \"gh-pages -d dist\"\n   }\n   ```\n4. Run the deploy command from your terminal:\n   ```bash\n   npm run deploy\n   ```\n   *This will compile your site and push the compiled static output directly to your `gh-pages` branch, bypassing GitHub Actions entirely!*\n\n#### Option B: Drag-and-Drop Static Files\n1. Build the applet here in AI Studio (which compiles successfully into the `dist/` folder).\n2. Download the project as a ZIP file from the top-right settings menu.\n3. On GitHub, create a branch named `gh-pages`.\n4. Go to that branch on github.com and directly drag-and-drop the contents of your `dist` folder into the repository.\n5. In your repository settings under **Settings > Pages**, set the source to deploy from the `gh-pages` branch."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 175906285
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
