  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Extracting CV Content**\n\nI\'ve got it - the primary focus is providing the text from the CV right away. It\'s a quick turnaround. The goal is a downloadable and printable PDF representation immediately. I am going to concentrate on immediate delivery.\n\n\n**Expanding Download Options**\n\nI am now focusing on expanding the options for users to obtain the extracted CV content. Beyond immediate display, I\'m considering providing downloadable versions in various formats: plain text, markdown, and perhaps even HTML, all directly generated from the extracted data. My goal is to integrate these download options seamlessly into the user\'s workflow, either through a download button or directly in the workspace. The aim is to create convenient download options so the user can easily copy, paste, or save it.\n\n\n**Adding Download Options**\n\nI\'m now thinking about adding new download options. It\'s time to make it easier for users to save the extracted content. I\'m planning to introduce a new button for downloading the text in plain text or Markdown format. This will give more utility to the extracted data. This is simple, yet powerful, and a great addition.\n\n\n**Analyzing Personal Information**\n\nI\'m now focusing on analyzing the information from this professional profile. I\'m extracting key data points: contact details, location, a concise summary of skills and experience, and a detailed breakdown of core competencies across systems, telecom, QA, and agility. I\'m concentrating on categorizing the strengths, to enable easy filtering and usage by any user.\n\n\n**Detailing Experience Highlights**\n\nI\'m now diving into the detailed work experience. I am compiling key highlights. This includes protocol testing across L1-L3, Selenium Grid, HP ALM, and JIRA. I am also working on management and roles: Project Management, Scrum Master, Business Analyst, SDLC/STLC processes, Agile Methodology, and CSPO. I\'m focusing on significant achievements like preventing billing leakage, mitigating SNMP trap storms, and curing mediation race conditions. My goal is to extract the details from the career chronology section.\n\n\n**Generating Markdown Output**\n\nI\'m now generating a direct download of the CV content in Markdown format (.md). The goal is to provide a clean, easily editable representation of the experience section. I\'ll focus on structuring the job title, date range, company, and responsibilities, as bullet points. I will include the education and certifications sections too. I plan to provide this in an easy-to-use format.\n\n\n**Implementing Download Buttons**\n\nI am now implementing new download buttons for Markdown (.md) and text (.txt) files directly within the user interface. I\'m focusing on adding these options to the `ResumeModal.tsx` file, specifically inserting the new buttons beneath the existing \"Export to PDF / Print\" button. I will implement the code insertion around lines 205-222, based on the file layout. The goal is to make the downloading of editable content extremely robust and useful.\n\n\n**Adding Download Buttons**\n\nI am now adding the download buttons for the plain text and Markdown resume versions. The implementation is straightforward. I\'ll add the necessary buttons within the `ResumeModal.tsx` file, with the download functionality defined client-side for ease of use. I aim to place them beneath the existing \"Close Preview\" button. The download will extract the content and provide it in a downloadable format.\n\n\n**Categorizing Strengths Now**\n\nI am now organizing the core competencies and experience highlights. My focus is on categorizing strengths: Systems & Telecom Core (customer provisioning, billing systems), QA & Agility (protocol testing, Selenium Grid, HP ALM), and Management & Roles (project management, Scrum Master). I will include key accomplishments and experiences, such as blocking billing leakage and mitigating SNMP trap storms. The goal is to facilitate easy filtering and application of these data points.\n\n\n**Highlighting Performance Achievements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on adding performance achievements to the CV extraction. I\'m highlighting key wins, like solving telemetry queue overflows and curing mediation race conditions. These details are important for demonstrating impact and value. I aim to provide specific examples of positive results.\n\n\n**Adding Experience Details**\n\nI am now adding the details from the work history, and the qualifications, including: my work at Tech Mahindra, Accenture, and Gapbridge Software. I\'m focusing on the experience, academic background, and certifications. I\'m extracting key data like dates, responsibilities, and specific roles. I am ensuring all data is saved as required.\n\n\n"
